  "changes": [
    "Existing native coefficient extraction shared by central Float and exact Gaussian-rational specialization. Central recurrence arithmetic is unchanged.",
    "compile_rows retains parallel exact_source_rows after existing exact denominator LCM, preserving full degree and exact nonzero sparse entries. Numerical parameters are specialized as stored exact dyadics; their physical uncertainty remains separate.",
    "Ordinary and epsilon charts use native ComplexBall coefficient construction and UnivariatePolynomial<FloatField<ComplexBall>> derivative/shift/product/subtraction to enclose the full exact-source differential defect. Registered-root assembly retains its explicit existing MPFR estimate scope.",
    "Native outward precision rescaling preserves exact stored dyadic Taylor coefficient values without letting an old storage precision unnecessarily limit evidence arithmetic. This does not promote input accuracy.",
    "Directed Float operations form disk majorants using a certified component one-norm radius and lower component denominator modulus. No new convolution, recurrence or transcendental interval arithmetic.",
    "Budgeted whole_segment_residual hook defaults to existing mandatory evidence. Rational owner requests precision only when enclosure width exceeds budget and dominates the central residual magnitude; genuine truncation and geometric denominator uncertainty remain step rejection.",
    "No acceptance tolerance relaxation. Strongly cancelling non-dyadic sources can still exhaust the working-derived local tolerance and must fail with a typed result."
  ],
